<!-- Implementation Notes -->
<div class="pa-card">
  <div class="pa-card__header">
    <h3>Implementation Notes</h3>
  </div>
  <div class="pa-card__body">
    <h4>Auto-Initialization</h4>
    <p>Add <code>data-multiselect</code> attribute to automatically initialize:</p>
    <pre><code>&lt;div data-multiselect
     data-options='[...]'
     data-search-placeholder="Search..."&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>

    <h4>Data Attributes</h4>
    <ul>
      <li><code>data-options</code> - JSON array of options</li>
      <li><code>data-search-placeholder</code> - Input placeholder text</li>
      <li><code>data-search-hint</code> - Optional hint text above input</li>
      <li><code>data-initial-values</code> - JSON array of pre-selected values</li>
      <li><code>data-allow-groups</code> - Enable/disable option groups (default: true)</li>
      <li><code>data-allow-select-all</code> - Show Select All button (default: true)</li>
      <li><code>data-allow-clear-all</code> - Show Clear All button (default: true)</li>
      <li><code>data-max-height</code> - Max dropdown height (default: 20rem)</li>
      <li><code>data-empty-message</code> - Custom empty state message</li>
    </ul>

    <h4>Option Structure</h4>
    <pre><code>{
  "value": "unique-id",      // Required: Unique identifier
  "label": "Display Text",   // Required: Main text
  "icon": "🔥",              // Optional: Icon or emoji
  "subtitle": "Description", // Optional: Subtitle text
  "group": "Group Name",     // Optional: Group label
  "disabled": false          // Optional: Disable selection
}</code></pre>

    <h4>Programmatic Initialization</h4>
    <pre><code>const multiselect = new MultiSelect(element, {
  options: [
    {value: 'js', label: 'JavaScript'},
    {value: 'py', label: 'Python'}
  ],
  searchPlaceholder: 'Search...',
  searchHint: 'Type to search',
  allowGroups: true,
  allowSelectAll: true,
  allowClearAll: true,
  maxHeight: '20rem',
  emptyMessage: 'No results found',
  onSelect: (option) => {
    console.log('Selected:', option);
  },
  onDeselect: (option) => {
    console.log('Deselected:', option);
  },
  onChange: (selectedOptions) => {
    console.log('Changed:', selectedOptions);
  }
});</code></pre>

    <h4>Public API</h4>
    <pre><code>// Get selected options
const selected = multiselect.getSelected();

// Set selected values programmatically
multiselect.setSelected(['js', 'py']);

// Destroy instance
multiselect.destroy();</code></pre>

    <h4>Size Modifiers</h4>
    <p>Add size classes to the container element:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>ml--xs</code> - Extra small</li>
      <li><code>ml--sm</code> - Small</li>
      <li>(no modifier) - Default size</li>
      <li><code>ml--lg</code> - Large</li>
      <li><code>ml--xl</code> - Extra large</li>
    </ul>

    <h4>Floating UI Integration</h4>
    <p>The component uses <a href="https://floating-ui.com/" target="_blank">Floating UI</a> for intelligent dropdown positioning with automatic flipping and shifting to stay within the viewport.</p>
  </div>
</div>

